## Remove grey rounded background box for metadata loading spinner and status

Context:
On the Unity Catalog (Data Assets) page, `#metadataStatus` was wrapped in a
Bootstrap `.alert alert-secondary` rounded box. During initial load and status
polling, the spinner and "Loading data assets…" text rendered inside that grey
box. Loading spinners must sit seamlessly on the card surface without a
separate background or rounded box container.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_metadata.html
   Removed `class="alert alert-secondary"` from `#metadataStatus`. The status
   container is now seamless (`class="mb-4"`) with inline muted flex styling.
2. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-metadata.js
   `loadMetadataStatus` now renders loading, loaded, empty, and error states
   cleanly without `alert` box classes (`statusDiv.className = 'mb-4'`,
   clean icons, no rounded background box).
3. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   Documented the explicit rule: never wrap spinners and loading text in a
   separate background container (e.g. `alert-secondary`, rounded grey boxes,
   or bordered wells). Spinners must sit seamlessly on their parent surface.

